# Build context is the repository root; only what the image needs goes in.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.vite
.git
.github
.claude
.playwright-mcp
.idea
.vscode
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Documentation (LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md stay: the image ships both)
docs

# Eval answers, results and agent setups: the image needs the corpus models
# (`analyzr seed`) and the golden value chains (`analyzr seed --value-chains`) only,
# and an agent with shell access to the container must not find the expected
# relations or placements there. A chain file holds steps only, without links:
# the same document an agent reads over MCP once a project is seeded with it.
# expected-placements.yaml, the READMEs and the validator stay out; CI's docker
# job checks that no expected*, *.md, *.mjs or *.jsonl file is under /app/eval.
eval/corpus/*/expected.yaml
eval/corpus/*/README.md
eval/corpus/*/spec
eval/recordings
eval/reports
eval/value-chains/**
!eval/value-chains/*/value-chain.vc.json
examples
plugins
.claude-plugin
